# Jaguar XE (X760) four-door saloon, 2015-2024.
#
# The compact executive Jaguar on the D7a aluminium platform: short front
# overhang, long bonnet, rising beltline, narrow swept headlamps with the
# J-shaped daytime light, a rounded-rectangular mesh grille, a strong flank
# crease through the door handles and a chrome fender blade behind the front
# wheel. The pre-facelift 2015-2019 body is modelled; the 2019 facelift
# changed the bumper intakes, lamps and rear bumper.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_XE
#
# Dimensions 4.672 x 1.850 x 1.416 m, wheelbase 2.835 m. The Chinese
# long-wheelbase XEL is not the UK car and is not modelled.
#
# Shape reference: no true level side elevation was available. The side image
# is a front three-quarter about 45 degrees off the centre line, the most
# side-on XE found; the flank is reconciled against the front and rear
# three-quarters within the published dimensions. The limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: no Jaguar UK document was retrieved, so no factory paint name is
# claimed (grade d). White, Black, Blue and Silver are plain colour names; the
# four most common UK colours of the period, not factory wording. Weights 6, 5,
# 5, 4, total 20, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 240 km/h. Comfort 95/473, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 95. Classes 2,3.
# Dates 2015-2024 production, road tail staggered 2038-2041.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-xe.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-xe.dae. References: citycars/references/jaguar-xe/
# (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 4.0).
#
# Accepted deviations: no true side elevation exists; the side image is a front
# three-quarter about 45 degrees off, and the flank was reconciled against both
# three-quarters and the published dimensions. The rear follows the photographs:
# two adjacent exhaust tips and no continuous chrome bar between the lamps. Lamp,
# grille and wheel detail is simplified at sprite scale. The pre-facelift body is
# modelled.


obj=citycar
